       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You can titrate to 10 mg after 1\u20132 weeks if needed.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if you intend it. I'd need you to confirm that, and I'll add a note with the rationale.\n\nIf blood pressure is still uncontrolled at 10 mg, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred to going above 10 mg.\n\nTell me which option and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
